      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/soon-available-rineloricaria-aurata/",
      "html": "<p>Rineloricaria aurata occurs in Paraguay. Whiptail catfishes destined for export are mostly collected from the Paraguay River not far from the capital Asunción, where three species can be expected: R. aurata, R. lanceolata and R. parva.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/soon-available-rineloricaria-aurata/",
      "html": "<p>A sandy bottom is necessary, as the fish burrow.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/soon-available-rineloricaria-aurata/",
      "html": "<p>More than the other two species, R. aurata tends to burrow. Without a sandy bottom these fishes do not feel well.</p>"
    }
  ],
